-- title:
--   Fibre-sum law for f over a value c₀ on the base line
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$, $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ a ring homomorphism, `data` a `ModularPolynomialData q` satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr`, and $h\alpha,h\beta$ the integrality of the two degeneracy maps from level $1$ to level $q$; let $P$ be a `PlaceSpecialization` for these data. Let $K_1$ be a field of characteristic zero with $\overline{\mathbb Q}\subseteq K_1\subseteq F:=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar (1*q)`, the extension $F/K_1$ finite and separable, and let $R$ be a level-one prolongation pair for $P$ with Gauss transport over $K_1$, so that $V:=R.\mathrm{gaussBase}\,K_1$ is the pullback of $R.R_1.\mathrm{integers}$ to $K_1$. Let $y,f\in F$ lie in the integers of both $R.R_1$ and $R.R_2$ and be integral over $V$, and suppose the order $S:=V[y,f]$ contains `jFun` and `jqFun`, spans $F$ over $K_1$, and that the two residue fields `ResOne`, `ResTwo` of the pair have degrees over the residue field of $V$ summing to $[F:K_1]$, each being generated by an element of $S$ whose image under $\rho_1$, resp. $\rho_2$, has Laurent expansion `jqModC` over the residue field of $A$. Let $e_1\colon \overline{\mathbb Q}(X)\simeq K_1$ be an $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra isomorphism with $x:=e_1X\in V$ whose residue is transcendental over the residue field of $A$, and let $r_1,r_2\in k[X]$ have positive degree, with $R.\mathrm{residue}_1(x)$ and $R.\mathrm{residue}_2(x)$ corresponding under `ratFuncEquivCharLOneC` to $r_1$ and $r_2$ respectively, and $\operatorname{finrank}$ of `ResOne`, `ResTwo` equal to $\deg r_1$, $\deg r_2$. Assume the residues of $f$ at $R.R_1$ and $R.R_2$ are nonzero, and let $D$ be a divisor of $F/\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $D(W)=\operatorname{ord}_W f$ for every place $W$. Then for every $c_0\in k$, the sum of $D$ over those $W$ in the support of $D$ for which some $a\in A$ has $\mathrm{red}\,a=c_0$ and $\operatorname{ord}_W(x-a)>0$ equals $\sum_a \operatorname{ord}_{[a]}\!\big(R.\mathrm{residue}_1 f\big)+\sum_b \operatorname{ord}_{[b]}\!\big(R.\mathrm{residue}_2 f\big)$, where $a$ runs over the distinct roots of $r_1-c_0$ in $k$, $b$ over those of $r_2-c_0$, and $[\cdot]$ denotes the place `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint` of the genus-zero field `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` attached to a point of $k$.
--
--   This is the summed pencil law: the total order of $f$ along the fibre of the coordinate $x$ over a value $c_0$ in characteristic $q$ is expressed through the two residual rational functions $r_1,r_2$ of $x$ and the residues of $f$ on the two prolongations of the pair. It feeds the downstream pencil statements `sum_filter_value_eq_ord_add_sum_roots` and `sum_filter_value_eq_sum_roots_add_pencil`, which transport divisors of the level-$q$ modular function field to characteristic $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_PlaceSpecialization_LevelOneProlongationPair_sum_filter_value_eq_sum_roots_add.lean

